Third-party material in the Voice style
=======================================

The directories below start with "_", so Vale does not load them as rules.
Rules in this style extend them by name (for example
`extends: Voice._voices.Puffery`) and change only what this style decides
differently. Update a copy by replacing the file from the upstream source and
running the tests.

_dictionaries/
  en_US.dic and en_US.aff from the SCOWL/ESDB Hunspell dictionaries,
  release 2026.02.25 (hunspell-en_US-2026.02.25.zip,
  https://github.com/en-wl/wordlist/releases). Six entries that the
  commit-time secret scan's vocabulary policy rejects were removed from
  en_US.dic, and its word count lowered to match; prose that uses them is
  reported as misspelled. The copyright and license terms are in
  _dictionaries/README_en_US.txt.

_voices/
  Rules from Voices by Joseph Kato (https://github.com/jdkato/voices), commit
  5409079d0abc1f63cbb1d329731b72444fbd5bea, MIT License. The upstream test
  cases were removed from each file, since they assert the upstream rule
  names. _voices/LICENSE and _voices/NOTICE are the upstream files; several
  rules derive from no-ai-slop by Peter Yang, MIT License.

_aitells/
  Rules from vale-ai-tells by Tony Burns
  (https://github.com/tbhb/vale-ai-tells), release v1.37.0, MIT License.
  _aitells/LICENSE is the upstream license.
